    description: "Concept audit 2026-10-21/22 (pinned dev e9215548f6; write-up ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept_audit_10212026/concept-audit-vocabulary-since-0923_10222026.md). F3. Anchors are mandated (spec section 9 'src anchoring', INV-foluz / INV-nopoh) and stay. Recommended verdict KEEP + DOCUMENT: write the contract (src = the code unit whose execution makes the call: function/method, or an anchor for code outside any function, with WHEN it runs: import, first use, every construction) into the spec / an ADR-0023 amendment, and fix spec drift: docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:1205 says rust/java/kotlin/swift/ruby/c/cpp/scala/lua are 'still missing' anchoring (all anchor now) and omits type-body anchoring; :123 says file-anchored flows are always structural (false since WI-nilir). Must land before WI-mifag (test-only reachability reads calls.src as callers). Sibling consumer fixes are filed separately."  # 59d9
